WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.933 line:15%
Listen,
(crowd claps)

2
00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:02.880 line:15%
not all heroes wear capes.

3
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.000
But this past year, we certainly learned

4
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.850
that many of them wear white coats.

5
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:11.050
Doctors are among the people who have put their own lives

6
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.980
on the line to save those around them.

7
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.650
However, "The New York Times" reports

8
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.650
that only 5% of American physicians are Black

9
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:25.110
and only 2% of them are Black women.

10
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.220
And disease does not discriminate,

11
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.390
and nor should the healthcare field.

12
00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.780
And that's why a team of doctors

13
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.590
from North Carolina started a foundation,

14
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.750
called White Coats Black Doctors,

15
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.110
to encourage more Black men and women

16
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.620
to study medicine and to provide financial aid

17
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.830
to those Black medical students.

18
00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.900
So here to tell us about it are its two founders.

19
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.420
Please welcome Internal Medicine Dr. Jenay Powell

20
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.204
and OB/GYN, Dr. Celeste Green.

21
00:00:57.204 --> 00:00:59.018
(crowd claps)

22
00:00:59.018 --> 00:01:00.578
Hi, ladies!

23
00:01:00.578 --> 00:01:05.578
Hi, thank you so much for having us.

24
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.800
Dr. Powell, what was the moment

25
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.230
that inspired you to just start this foundation?

26
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.580
So back in 2015, a group of medical students traveled

27
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.350 line:15%
to New Orleans for a medical education conference.

28
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.970 line:15%
And on our way down there, actually, Dr. Green had the idea

29
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.779
to print up these t-shirts, basically from a mall kiosk,

30
00:01:29.779 --> 00:01:32.580
that had White Coats Black Doctors on it.

31
00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.750
Which was the name of our GroupMe

32
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.250
that our medical school class sort of communicated

33
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.230
about things going on at the school.

34
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.670
And so, we had these shirts on and basically it was a way

35
00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.450
for us to sort of celebrate our achievements thus far

36
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.980
and sort of let everyone know who we were.

37
00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.610
And so, once we all had the shirts on

38
00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.220
and we're literally walking down Bourbon Street,

39
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.730
we had bystanders, fellow medical students

40
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.550
that were attending the conference, physicians,

41
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.877
and just other people that kept stopping us and were like,

42
00:02:03.877 --> 00:02:05.980
"Hey, where did you get these t-shirts?

43
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.150
We really love them.

44
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.980
Can we have some, can we buy them?"

45
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.100 line:15%
And so, we started sort of taking down names and numbers

46
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.110 line:15%
and figured out how to get the t-shirts out there.

47
00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.696 line:15%
And then, once the money started coming in,

48
00:02:17.696 --> 00:02:20.530 line:15%
the five of us founders sort of sat down and thought

49
00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.770 line:15%
about what it was that we wanted to do with the money.

50
00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.430
And I think all five of us,

51
00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.210
being first generation physicians and having looked back

52
00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.100
on our road and trajectories into medicine,

53
00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.840
really thought that starting this foundation

54
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.110
would be a great way to give back to other young students

55
00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:40.090
like us, which we do in the form of scholarships.

56
00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.050
I love that and it just also shows,

57
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.470
if you build it, they will come.

58
00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.300
If you put a logo on it, it's real.

59
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.270
And this is just such a great way

60
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.513
to incentivize people to just start.

61
00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:56.340
Dr. Green, why do you think that there is such a lack

62
00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.423
of Black women and male doctors?

63
00:03:00.338 --> 00:03:04.190
I think it's a great question and my belief is

64
00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:07.710 line:15%
that it's really only due to a lack of opportunity

65
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.560 line:15%
and a lack of support or encouragement.

66
00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.320 line:15%
And it's not just my belief, there's data to support that.

67
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.680
We know that Black students, young students,

68
00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.370
school age children, they're more likely

69
00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:23.720
to be at schools with limited resources.

70
00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.770
They are less likely to be enrolled

71
00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.230
in STEM courses or summer enrichment programs.

72
00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:32.330
That pipeline, as we call it in medicine

73
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:36.288
and medical education, the pipeline to medical education

74
00:03:36.288 --> 00:03:39.290
is not a very continuous one

75
00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.800
when it comes to minority students.

76
00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.540
That can be because of lack of opportunity

77
00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.200
and lack of access but also, I think

78
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.030
what's hugely important is the lack of support

79
00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.890
and lack of encouragement for that little Black girl

80
00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.750
or little Black boy who might not see a Black physician

81
00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.220
for their entire upbringing.

82
00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.630 line:15%
And then when they go to the doctor as a young adult,

83
00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.070 line:15%
they might not have a Black physician.

84
00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.290 line:15%
And who can they turn to for encouragement

85
00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.157 line:15%
or who can they turn to to say,

86
00:04:08.157 --> 00:04:10.270 line:15%
"How do I get into your shoes" if they don't see it?

87
00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.660
And so for us, for White Coats Black Doctors,

88
00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.370
the phrase that I like to say is

89
00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.710
that our visibility is our activism.

90
00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:21.170
And so being out in public wearing our t-shirts

91
00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.300
and our polos and selling sweatshirts

92
00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.240
and all those things, it's not just to make money.

93
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.160
It's to make sure that there are people

94
00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.572
who see us and know this is achievable.

95
00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.420
(sighs) Well, I mean, you've supported hundreds

96
00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.640
of men and women on their way

97
00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.940
to wearing white coats like you.

98
00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.410
And we actually have a special message

99
00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.830
from some of those doctors and medical students

100
00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.803
that you've inspired, take a look.

101
00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.930 line:15%
I want to thank White Coats Black Doctors

102
00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.490 line:15%
for allowing me to connect with doctors

103
00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.730
that I can relate to and who look like me.

104
00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.480 line:15%
You can't be what you can't see,

105
00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.480 line:15%
and so organizations like White Coats Black Doctors

106
00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.820
are so important for increasing representation.

107
00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.130 line:15%
Having that kind of extended support system

108
00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.160 line:15%
is so important.

109
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.620
I wanna thank them for the award back in 2017

110
00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.570
that completely covered the cost of my MCAT.

111
00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.410
That was a major financial burden

112
00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.010
that was lifted off of my shoulders.

113
00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:20.070 line:15%
The match day is coming up next week,

114
00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.250 line:15%
where I'll actually get to find out

115
00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.420
where I'll be starting my career

116
00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.460
as the first physician in my family.

117
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.520
Once again, thank you.

118
00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.180
Thank you, White Coats Black Doctors,

119
00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.850 line:15%
for valuing my perspective

120
00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.330 line:15%
as a future healthcare administrator.

121
00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.880 line:15%
It is because of my engagement

122
00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.670 line:15%
with White Coats Black Doctors

123
00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:41.090
that I will be the very first Black physician in my family.

124
00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.910
Despite everything that's going on with COVID-19,

125
00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.496
I would not trade my role as a doctor for the world.

126
00:05:47.496 --> 00:05:49.130
(crowd claps)

127
00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:52.270
I'm looking at all the people in your video and you guys,

128
00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:56.440 line:15%
you're all so wonderful and beautiful and inspiring,

129
00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:00.010 line:15%
and you are helping people see it.

130
00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.160
And this is so important, what you are doing,

131
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.337
and we're all so inspired by it.

132
00:06:05.337 --> 00:06:09.830
And you're bringing that diversity gap

133
00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:13.700
to the medical field and trying to close it

134
00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:18.160
and give people that visual that they belong, too.

135
00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.050
And I wanna thank our producer, Haryana,

136
00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:25.200
who got $5,000 to donate to your foundation

137
00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.220
to help support your medical students.

138
00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.294
And I wanna match it, so that'll be $10,000

139
00:06:31.294 --> 00:06:32.390
(crowd claps and cheers)

140
00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:36.610
to the White Coats and Black Doctors.

141
00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:37.854
That is incredible.

142
00:06:37.854 --> 00:06:40.060
(stammers) I'm at a loss for words.

143
00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.500
Thank you for the opportunity to talk

144
00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.123
about this passion project of ours.

145
00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.350
It's changed our lives.

146
00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.720
For me, it's been probably one

147
00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.470
of the biggest things I've ever accomplished

148
00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.350
and one of my most proudest accomplishments.

149
00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.750
And so, it is really special to be recognized for that.

150
00:06:58.750 --> 00:06:59.750
Thank you.

151
00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:04.460
Of course, and we wanna put White Coats Black Doctors

152
00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.700 line:15%
up on our website, so that if anybody would like to donate

153
00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.560 line:15%
and help further this cause of what Dr. Powell

154
00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.480 line:15%
and Dr. Green are doing, I think this is a vital mission

155
00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:20.090
and I'm blown away by the people that you have had rise up.

156
00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:21.410
You're just incredible.

157
00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.810
And we're honored to be able to share the spotlight

158
00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.330
with you, shine a light on what you're doing

159
00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.440
and help support it, and we wanna continue that.

160
00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.549
You're incredible.

161
00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:32.267
(crowd claps and cheers)

162
00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:33.634
Thank you.

163
00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:35.030
Thank you so much.

164
00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.151
Thank you so much!

165
00:07:36.151 --> 00:07:38.734 line:15%
(bright music)

